<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35261" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-mūnĭo</span></b> ,
			īvi or ĭi, ītum, 4,
			v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to fortify completely</i>, <i>to
				finish fortifying</i> (not in Cic. or Cæs.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quae munimenta incohaverat, permunit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					30, 16</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">permunitas Athenas esse,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Just.
					2, 15, 9</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, in gen., <i>to fortify
				completely</i> or <i>thoroughly</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">castris permunitis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 7,
					16</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">locorum opportuna permunivit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					4, 24</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">2, 7</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Just.
					24, 7, 8</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>